tudents. Serves as a Campus Security Authority (CSA). *The Master's in Public Health is pending SACSCOC approval. Essential Duties and Responsibilities :  100% Teaching:   Teach online undergraduate and/or graduate Public Health courses as assigned. Design, prepare, and deliver course instruction in a fully online learning environment using the institution’s learning management system (Canvas). Develop and maintain course syllabi, instructional materials, assignments, and assessments aligned with course objectives and program standards. Facilitate an engaging online learning environment that supports student participation, interaction, and critical thinking. Maintain regular and timely communication with students in the online course environment. Evaluate student performance and provide timely, constructive feedback on assignments and assessments. Monitor and document student progress, including grading, attendance (as applicable), and academic reporting requirements. Utilize instructional technologies and multimedia tools to support effective online teaching and student engagement. Provide virtual academic support to students, including scheduled online office hours and course-related guidance. Adhere to university policies, academic integrity standards, and applicable accreditation requirements.    Other information:   Adjunct Faculty positions are temporary appointments, assigned per semester and on an as-needed basis.  These temporary appointments are for the Academic Year 2026-2027 sub-terms.  Required Qualifications:   Earned master’s degree in Public Health or a closely related field from an accredited university with a minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in Public Health or the teaching discipline. Demonstrated ability to teach undergraduate and/or graduate Public Health courses effectively. Effective written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills . Ability to utilize instructional technologies and learning management systems such as Canvas, to support course delivery and student engagement. Preferred Qualifications:   Earned doctorate/terminal degree (PhD, DrPH or a closely related field) from an accredited institution with graduate coursework appropriate to the teaching discipline.  Previous teaching experience in higher education, particularly in online or hybrid instructional format. Professional experience in Public Health practice, healthcare systems, health administration, community health, or related areas. Experience using Canvas or similar learning management systems. Relevant professional certifications such as CHES/MCHES or CPH. Expertise in one or more areas of Public Health instruction. Areas of Instructional Need The department seeks applicants with the ability to teach one or more courses in the following areas: Public Health Policy Health Promotion and Education Health Statistics/Biostatistics Program Planning and Evaluation Epidemiology Research Methods Non-Medical Drivers of Health Health Informatics Health Communication Public Health Capstone or Internship Courses Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities :  Knowledge and understanding of disciplinary subject matter at a level adequate for undergraduate and graduate-level instruction; written and oral communication skills sufficient to conduct effective teaching activities; ability to interact with students, staff, and faculty in a professional, collegial, and collaborative manner.  ***Commensurate with experience***   Application Procedure:   During the application process applicants have one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and Submit the application. Applicants will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once the application materials have been submitted via the \"Submit\" action.   Employment applications must include (required):   Completed online application   Cover Letter / Letter of Interest addressing qualifications    Curriculum Vitae or Resume   At least 3 current professional references and their full contact information   Unofficial transcripts               Applications received by Tarleton State University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. Incomplete applications will not be considered.   Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled.    Official transcripts must be received directly from each degree‐granting institution prior to a letter of appointment being issued.   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
